onesia, under construction since 2022 in East Kalimantan on the island of Borneo.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/nush-i-jan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nush-i-jan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Nush-i Jan</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Nush-i Jan (Tepe Nush-i Jan) is an archaeological site in western Iran, near Malayer in Hamadan Province, excavated by a British team under David Stronach from 1967.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/nusrat-al-din-abu-bakr"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nusrat-al-din-abu-bakr.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Nusrat al-Din Abu Bakr</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Nusrat al-Din Abu Bakr was atabeg of Azerbaijan from 1191 to 1210, a member of the Eldiguzid dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/nusrat-khan"><span class="enc-name">Nusrat Khan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Nusrat Khan was a general and minister of Alauddin Khalji, sultan of Delhi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/nutmeg"><span class="enc-name">Nutmeg</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Nutmeg is a spice obtained from the seed of a tree native to the Banda Islands in the Moluccas of present-day Indonesia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/nuuk"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nuuk.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Nuuk</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Nuuk is the capital of Greenland, on the south-west coast at the mouth of a large fjord system.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/nuwa-mbaguta"><span class="enc-name">Nuwa Mbaguta</span><span cla